  "name": "Josh Mate's Better Backpacks",
  "slug": "josh-mates-better-backpacks",
  "teaser": "Makes backpacks bigger in a balanced way",
  "thumbnail": "https://forge-static.sp-tarkov.com/mods/772.jpg",
  "downloads": 113237,
  "favourites_count": 0,
  "description": "<h3><strong>Josh Mate’s Better Backpacks</strong></h3>\n<h4><strong>Description</strong></h4>\n<p>Makes Backpacks bigger while still staying in line with Vanilla gameplay balance based on price / rarity / weight</p>\n<p><strong>Changes</strong></p>\n<p>- All single grid backpacks have had their sizes increased by about 40%</p>\n<p>- Boss bags (Birds eye radio / Sanitar / Partisan) have been made significantly larger to fit their boss status</p>\n<p>- Bags with multiple grids were increased by less to prevent UI grid overlap issues</p>\n<p>- The field medic bag had its item restrictions removed</p>\n<h4><strong>How to Configure this mod</strong></h4>\n<p>- All backpacks come pre-edited to new bigger but balanced sizes. Just install and play</p>\n<p>- You can edit the values in Mod.ts to your liking</p>\n<p>- Increasing bag sizes too much can cause UI grid over lap issues</p>\n<p>- Increasing bag sizes on backpacks with multiple frame grids can cause UI issues</p>\n<h4><strong>Installation</strong></h4>\n<p>Move the mod’s “user” folder into your SPT AKI folder that contains your user folder.</p>\n<h4><strong>Special Thanks</strong></h4>\n<p>Special thanks to <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/user/3407-nootropix/\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Nootropix</a> for the original mod framework<br />\nSpecial thanks to <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/user/10639-jjbeanson/\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">JJBeanson</a> for adding the IDs for some missing back packs<br />\nSpecial thanks to <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/user/74614-tedthepraimortis/\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">tedthepraimortis</a> for adding the IDs for the new 3.10 back packs</p>\n",
